course: dictionary
lesson: 4665
title: Hogmanay: Scotland's New Year
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hogmanay is a noun, and it is a name for a celebration. Read the context to find its meaning. «Hogmanay is Scottish New Year» tells you it is a Scottish celebration of the new year.
explain: Context also tells you what happens at Hogmanay. Fireworks, street parties in Edinburgh and singing «Auld Lang Syne» at midnight are all clues. They help you picture the whole night, even if you have never been to Scotland.
explain: Some words belong to one place or culture. When a word like Hogmanay is new to you, use the clues around it first, then check a dictionary to confirm.
fact: Hogmanay means New Year's Eve in Scotland, on 31 December.
fact: «Hogmanay is Scottish New Year» tells you it is a Scottish celebration.
fact: At Hogmanay, many people sing «Auld Lang Syne» at midnight.
fact: First-footing is a custom: the first visitor to a home after midnight is said to bring luck.
fact: Ideally, a lucky first-footer is tall and dark-haired, and carries coal, shortbread or a gift.
exercise: «Hogmanay is Scottish New Year.» What does Hogmanay mean? | *New Year's Eve in Scotland | A birthday party in Australia | A type of Scottish shortbread | A Welsh word for darling
exercise: What is first-footing? | A firework made in Edinburgh | A dance at a street party | *A custom where the first visitor after midnight is said to bring luck | A way of cooking shortbread
exercise: Which things might a lucky first-footer carry? | Umbrella and a map | *Coal, shortbread or a gift | Fireworks and a flag | Crisps and a football
test: «Hogmanay has fireworks, street parties and singing at midnight.» What does this tell you? | A type of food | *It is a big celebration with lots happening | A sports match | A quiet day at school
test: A child reads «Hogmanay is Scottish New Year.» Which country celebrates it? | Australia | England | Wales | *Scotland
exam: If you do not know what Hogmanay means, what is the best way to work it out? | Guess from the sound of the word | *Use the clues around it, then check in a dictionary | Ask for a different word to be used instead | Skip the whole text and never come back to it
